132	FACTS.md:97
133	- **The `XXX` expected-failure mechanism in `compiler_tests/` and `library_tests/` can express a compile-stage failure only, and a run-time defect needs two `.test` files** (`compile-ladder/rung-tryatomic/`). `shouldFail` comes from the `.test` file name (`FileTests.java:1049`) and reaches every stage the file drives (`:1169-1186`), so an `XXX` file that carries `link` or `compile` demands that the compile fail (`:394-414`), while an unsatisfied `run_out_*` verdict fails whatever `shouldFail` says (`:605-610`, `:654-656`; `pass`/`PASS` is the default check, `:276-282`). A compiles-but-crashes defect is therefore two `.test` files over one component, a plain-named one driving `link` and an `XXX`-named one driving `run` with a marker the failing run prints; a refusal is one compile test. Run in one JVM (`junit.sh`'s `ONE_JVM=1`, `compile-ladder/climb-batch-N/merged-tests/junit.sh`), the compile and link tests run before the run tests (`FileTests.java:1114-1121`).
134	
135	FACTS.md:104
136	- **An `XXX` compile test pinned by `compile_err_contains` whose program compiles is reported as a wrong failure, not a missing one** (`compile-ladder/rung-unknown-size-arm/probes/pre-edit-tests.txt`). The harness evaluates the check key whether or not the command failed, so a missed key fails with "Saw wrong failure" even when the compile exited 0 (`tests/unit_tests/FileTests.java:394-412`); "Missing expected failure" appears only with no key or a met one. Either way the test is red. A compile that throws is checked on its `exception` key, " OK Saw expected exception" (`:342-366`).
137	
138	FACTS.md:98
139	- **A thrown `CompilerError` takes a third path through the test harness, keyed on the `tests=` name, with check stream `compile_exception_*`** (`compile-ladder/climb-batch-2/repair/`). A `sayWhat` wall returns a `CompilerError` (`CodeGen.java:1551-1553`), a `RuntimeException` that `Shell.compileWithErrorHandling` does not catch (`Shell.java:904-915`), so it reaches `FileTests.java:342`'s `catch (Throwable ex)`, which keys the expected failure on the `.test` file's `tests=` value (`:351`, `:82`, `:1169-1176`): the `XXX` prefix goes on the component name. The stream holds `ex.toString()` (`:136`, `:349-350`), so the key is `compile_exception_contains`; pinned, the file is green (` OK Saw expected exception`, `:352-366`) and red when the wall falls or moves to another exception. First used by `compiler_tests/XXXTryAtomicCodegenRungB.test` (row 353).
140	
141	FACTS.md:105
142	- **The checker-count and distance stages read only the compiler's phases, so an edit to the test corpora, the texts or walk's evaluator and natives cannot move them** (`coordinator/climb-batch-workflow.md`, "Rules weighed by what they cost against what they protect", item 5). Both stages run `Shell.compilerPhases` with `PhaseOrder.compilerPhaseOrder` (`coordinator/tools/checker-count/WorldFlip.java:42`, `coordinator/tools/distance/DistanceMulti.java:64`; `ProjectFortress/src/com/sun/fortress/compiler/phases/PhaseOrder.java:137-147`, `ENVGEN` not in it), which reads no test, text or record. Outside `interpreter/`, walk's evaluator classes are named only by walk's commands in `Shell.java` (`:607-621`, `:1221`), by `ENVGEN`'s `compiler/environments/`, as field types of the exception classes and in the unused `compiler/codegen/Common.java`, and walk's natives only in the library's strings, which walk resolves. That is by reading, and four runs on an interpreter-only edit agree with it. The batch script acts on it by its `STAGE_BLIND` rule: a rung all of whose paths are under `explorations/`, `Specification/`, `Documentation/`, a test corpus, `interpreter/evaluator/`, `interpreter/glue/` or the test harness (`ProjectFortress/src/com/sun/fortress/tests/`, named outside its package only by `Shell.java`'s `junit` command, `:55` and `:1086`) runs neither stage and says so with the paths, and its skeptic checks the paths against the branch's diff (check 10); the gate measures both on the merged tree either way.
